{"comment_text": {"ja74:0.1": "", "ja74:0.2": "", "ja74:0.3": "", "ja74:0.4": "", "ja74:1.1": "While the verse speaks only of trees, the story says that the deities who live in trees are advised to dwell only in those clustered together in the forest. Some deities, however, greedy for human offerings, set up home in trees worshiped as shrines by villages. ", "ja74:1.2": "", "ja74:1.3": "", "ja74:1.4": "", "ja74:2.1": ""}, "html_text": {"ja74:0.1": "<article id='ja74'><header><ul><li class='division'>{}</li>", "ja74:0.2": "<li>{}</li>", "ja74:0.3": "<li>{}</li></ul>", "ja74:0.4": "<h1 class='sutta-title'>{}</h1></header>", "ja74:1.1": "<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja74:1.2": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja74:1.3": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span>", "ja74:1.4": "<span class='verse-line'>{}</span></p></blockquote>", "ja74:2.1": "<p class='endsutta'>{}</p></article>"}, "root_text": {"ja74:0.1": "Jātaka ", "ja74:0.2": "Ekakanipāta ", "ja74:0.3": "Varuṇavagga ", "ja74:0.4": "4. Rukkhadhammajātaka ", "ja74:1.1": "“Sādhū sambahulā ñātī, ", "ja74:1.2": "api rukkhā araññajā; ", "ja74:1.3": "Vāto vahati ekaṭṭhaṁ, ", "ja74:1.4": "brahantampi vanappatin”ti. ", "ja74:2.1": "Rukkhadhammajātakaṁ catutthaṁ. "}, "translation_text": {"ja74:0.1": "Stories of Past Lives 74 ", "ja74:0.2": "The Book of the Ones ", "ja74:0.3": "The Warding Tree ", "ja74:0.4": "The Law of Trees: a past life story ", "ja74:1.1": "It is well for the many relatives, ", "ja74:1.2": "the trees born in the forest. ", "ja74:1.3": "The wind sweeps off one standing alone, ", "ja74:1.4": "even the enormous lord of the forest. ", "ja74:2.1": ""}, "reference_text": {"ja74:0.1": "", "ja74:0.2": "", "ja74:0.3": "", "ja74:0.4": "", "ja74:1.1": "ms22J_163, msdiv74, pts-vp-pli1.329, sya27.24", "ja74:1.2": "", "ja74:1.3": "", "ja74:1.4": "", "ja74:2.1": "ms22J_164"}, "keys_order": ["ja74:0.1", "ja74:0.2", "ja74:0.3", "ja74:0.4", "ja74:1.1", "ja74:1.2", "ja74:1.3", "ja74:1.4", "ja74:2.1"]}